/target

# Python bytecode from tools/. Not a style preference: `rumor docs --check`
# requires every path in the tree to be mapped, and the coverage TEST
# (committed_tree_is_fully_mapped) fails on an unmapped one -- so a stray
# __pycache__ from running tools/check-workflows.py turns the whole suite red.
# It caught exactly that, after a `git add -A` swept one into a commit.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The Go binary from a bare `go build ./cmd/rumor`, which writes ./rumor into
# the repo root.
#
# WHAT THIS ENTRY DOES AND DOES NOT DO, corrected after run 142 proved the
# difference: it stops the artefact being COMMITTED. It does NOT stop
# `docs --check` failing on it, because the walk in internal/coverage never
# reads .gitignore -- it skips .git and target and nothing else. So a build into
# the tree still turns committed_tree_is_fully_mapped red whatever is listed
# here, which is exactly how run 142 went red on `rumor-bin`. The protection
# against that is building out-of-tree with -o, which ci.yml and the release
# both now do; this entry is hygiene, not the gate.
/rumor
